content.text:
The degradation comes from one fault: the `profile` service is down. Its failure reaches users through frontend's `/hotels` and `/recommendations` endpoints.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "profile",
      "fault_kind": "pod_unavailable",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT 'ab' p, metric, service_name, count(*) n, round(min(value),2) vmin, round(max(value),2) vmax FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE metric IN ('k8s.deployment.available','k8s.deployment.desired') AND service_name='profile' GROUP BY ALL UNION ALL SELECT 'n', metric, service_name, count(*), round(min(value),2), round(max(value),2) FROM normal_metrics WHERE metric IN ('k8s.deployment.available','k8s.deployment.desired') AND service_name='profile' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "Profile deployment available replicas stay at 0 for the whole incident window, versus 1 in normal."},
        {"kind": "log", "sql": "SELECT service_name, count(*) n FROM normal_logs WHERE service_name='profile' GROUP BY 1 UNION ALL SELECT 'abnormal_profile_logs', count(*) FROM abnormal_logs WHERE service_name='profile'", "claim": "Profile emitted about 2,418 logs in the normal period and none in the incident period."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT substr(CAST(time AS VARCHAR),1,16) mn, count(*) n, sum(CASE WHEN attr_status_code='Error' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) errs FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='frontend' AND span_name='profile.Profile/GetProfiles' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1", "claim": "Frontend's calls to profile.Profile/GetProfiles fail in every minute of the incident, mostly in tens of microseconds."}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {"from": "profile", "to": "frontend",
     "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT span_name, attr_span_kind, attr_status_code, count(*) n, sum(CASE WHEN attr_status_code='Error' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) errs FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='frontend' AND span_name IN ('profile.Profile/GetProfiles','HTTP /hotels','HTTP /recommendations') GROUP BY ALL ORDER BY 1,2", "claim": "GetProfiles client errors line up with HTTP /hotels and /recommendations 500s in frontend, which are otherwise healthy."}]
    },
    {"from": "frontend", "to": "frontend",
     "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT span_name, attr_http_response_status_code sc, count(*) n, sum(CASE WHEN attr_status_code='Error' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) errs FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='frontend' AND attr_span_kind='Server' GROUP BY ALL ORDER BY 1", "claim": "Frontend /hotels and /recommendations return HTTP 500 for nearly all requests; other endpoints return 200."}]
    }
  ]
}
```

The propagation list has a self-edge (`frontend` to `frontend`) that doesn't belong in the answer; the real chain is `profile` → `frontend`, and frontend is the user-facing tier. I also couldn't finish checking the profile pod's restart and uptime metrics (the query hit the output-size limit), so the "unavailable" label rests on the zero replica count and the missing logs and spans.
